{"t": 1794119733.8317652, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "\u26a0\ufe0f This change introduced a production regression.\n\nSentry issue: https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A \u2014 **ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit** (expected 1100, got 1099). First seen in release `ledger-worker@2026.11.3`; 2,201 events.\n\nCause: replacing the `Decimal` rounding in `worker/rates.py` with `int(...)` truncates toward zero instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, so converted totals come out 1 unit low and fail reconciliation.\n\nFix: `worker/rates.py` now multiplies with `Decimal` and quantizes to the nearest minor unit using `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Please cherry-pick/release a patch.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
